# Allowlist, not denylist. Claude Code writes credentials, session transcripts,
# and new state directories into this folder as it updates. Ignoring everything
# by default means a new state dir fails closed (unsynced) rather than open
# (published). Add new config here deliberately.

*

# --- Portable config: the stuff worth having on every machine ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json

!skills/
!skills/**
!agents/
!agents/**
!workflows/
!workflows/**
!hooks/
!hooks/**

# How often each skill gets used, one append-only file per machine so the
# logs never clash. Written by hooks/skill-usage.mjs.
!usage/
!usage/**

# Mods: panes and hooks that change Claude's own interface. Each is a plugin
# folder, loaded by CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS in settings.json.
!mods/
!mods/**

# The local config dashboard: server, page, and the skill folders you arrange
# in it. Runs from a fresh pull on any machine with Node.
!dashboard/
!dashboard/**

# Per-space working notes, written from the board's sidebar. Small, hand-kept,
# and worth having on every machine.
!board/
!board/**

# Pictures the README shows, such as the workflow diagram.
!docs/
!docs/**

# Installed by the twg CLI's own setup, not authored here. Each machine gets
# its own copy when it runs `twg setup`, so syncing them would fight the
# installer. Delete them with `rm -rf ~/.claude/skills/twg*` if unwanted.
skills/twg/
skills/twg-*/

# Written by the Claude app: its copies of the skills synced from the claude.ai
# account, and the ones it set aside. Each machine fetches its own.
skills/synced/
skills/.trash/

# Laid beside a mod by the engine at every load, naming the build that wrote
# them. Regenerated per machine, so syncing them would only ever conflict.
mods/*/.claude-plugin/types/

# --- Deliberately NOT synced, even though they sit next to the above ---
# .credentials.json   OAuth token
# .claude.json        (parent dir) user id, machine id, prompt history, MCP keys
# settings.local.json machine-local permission grants
# projects/           full session transcripts (~276MB)
# file-history/       snapshots of every file edited (~102MB)
# plugins/            cloned marketplaces; re-fetched on demand
# history.jsonl       your prompt history
# backups/ cache/ sessions/ shell-snapshots/ session-env/ paste-cache/
# tasks/ plans/ jobs/ daemon/ ide/ chrome/ downloads/ statsig/
